summary:
I fixed all four problems, and only in /home/user/ClinicalSageAI-2-replit/scripts/ci/check-purge-coverage.selftest.mjs (still untracked). The gate scripts/ci/check-purge-coverage.mjs, its baseline JSON and package.json are unchanged (git diff on the gate is 0 lines). The selftest now has 20 cases, up from 18, and runs in about 6 s.

1. Case 3 was credited to the wrong incident (medium). That case is now named 'FAILS on an unlisted parent of a purged table — a purged child does not reach its parent'. Its comment and header bullet describe only the FK-direction property and no longer mention the 2026-10-01 incident. A new paragraph, 'Also outside this gate's reach', sits next to 'Not asserted'. It says the gate checks which tables a purge reaches, never the order of the list. So an FK-order failure like the 23503 from deleting client_workspaces before projects (2ab30c93) passes both this gate and this selftest. That regression is guarded by tests/db/tenant-purge-artifact-records.dbtest.ts, which runs the real PURGE_CHILD_TABLES against a tenant that has a workspace and a project (I checked its seed: client_workspaces, then projects with client_workspace_id). Corrected wording for the report: case 3 covers FK direction only. It does not cover, and cannot detect, the 2026-10-01 order fix.

2. The false motivation (low). The header no longer says the failure branch 'has never been seen to fire'. It now lists the times it did fire:
- CI run 12751: governed_decision_transitions, after its cascade to projects was removed.
- CI run 12756: collab_presence and project_continuity_snapshots.
- CI run 12804: scheduled_job_claims.
- The P1-22 fix round (cd68fb65): organization_retention_settings. The red evidence is in docs/evidence/D6/2026-10-01-tranche-4/P1-22-org/red/.
Every one of those fired against whatever the live schema held that day, so nothing proved each detection path or the fail-closed branches; that is the stated reason now. Case 1 cites 12756 and 12804, and case 4 cites organization_retention_settings (cd68fb65).

3. The missing baseline was untested (low). New case 'FAILS closed on a missing baseline — every residue table counts as NEW'. It uses baseline: null and the default BASE_DDL. It expects exit 1, newTables exactly ['audit_logs'], the 'NEW org-keyed table(s) a tenant purge cannot reach' line and no ✅. It also checks that check mode did not create the baseline file.

4. The unprovisioned check was pinned only loosely (low). The fixture is now a partly provisioned database: organizations, users and projects exist, documents does not, plus an org-keyed table nothing reaches (adverse_events). It must say 'this database is not provisioned' and must not print '✅' or 'NEW org-keyed'. A second new case uses a fully empty database, with the same assertions.

Mutation checks: each mutant was a copy in the scratchpad, run with SELFTEST_GATE_PATH. All 16 were killed:
- missing baseline treated as `{ tables: residue }` (the reported mutant): only the new missing-baseline case fails;
- the probe weakened to `n < 2` (the reported mutant), `< 3` or `< 1`: only the partly-provisioned case fails each time;
- FKs followed in both directions: only case 3 fails;
- confdeltype check dropped, so any FK counts: cases 2 and 5 fail;
- organizations seeded as if it were deleted: case 4 fails;
- any table with a cascading FK counted as reached: cases 4 and 5 fail;
- the cascade followed one hop only: 10 cases fail, because document_versions is named NEW. I checked this is the two-hop property and not a crash;
- views counted as tables: 10 cases fail;
- comments not stripped before the scan: 12 cases fail;
- vault entries silently dropped: the first clean ('quiet') case fails;
- an uninterpretable entry silently dropped: its case fails;
- no carry-forward on --write-baseline: the write-baseline case fails;
- placeholder URL accepted: its case fails;
- NEW residue only warning instead of failing: 6 cases fail.
The runner is at /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ClinicalSageAI-2-replit/c90fcd29-2b71-5a17-91df-9b8d668d28ca/scratchpad/pc-mutants/run.mjs. The selftest left no temp directories behind.
